{"name":"Faint of Heart","hex":"#f1aaa8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"faint of heart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fainthearted."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Timid people considered as a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faint_of_heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heroes in the City of Dope","blocks":[{"text":"Heroes in the City of Dope is the first collaborative studio album by Zion I and The Grouch. It was released on Om Records on October 10, 2006. It peaked at number 29 on the Billboard Heatseekers Albums chart, as well as number 34 on the Independent Albums chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Heroesinthecityofdope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heroes_in_the_City_of_Dope","wikidata":"Q5743210"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/92/Heroesinthecityofdope.jpg/250px-Heroesinthecityofdope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Heroesinthecityofdope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp